From: AresOS
Subject: [PATCH] no bindings while the input-capture layer holds the keyboard

AresOS: our own change to labwc 0.9.6 (package 321, step 1c), applied after
0001. Nothing like it is upstream: labwc has no way to switch its bindings off
for a layer-shell surface (no keyboard-shortcuts-inhibit, and ToggleKeybinds
works per window).

While aresos-input-portal captures input for another machine (Deskflow), its
layer-shell surface holds the keyboard exclusively, but labwc still ran its
own bindings first: Alt+F4 closed a local window, Alt+Tab started the window
switcher, which then ate keys. With this patch, while a layer surface whose
namespace is "aresos-input-barrier" has exclusive keyboard focus:

- only keybinds marked allowWhenInhibited="yes" run (a new keybind attribute,
  modelled on allowWhenLocked); every other key goes to the surface;
- no mousebind runs: buttons and scroll go to the surface;
- a keybind pressed before the surface took the keyboard runs no on-release
  action, and its repeat runs nothing; a drag begun before is dropped;
- menu and window-switcher keys are not handled;
- switching the virtual terminal works as before.

seat_bindings_inhibited() is the one test. It reads the state at each event
and keeps none of its own. Layer surfaces with any other namespace, and all
windows, keep labwc's bindings as they were. Touch and tablet-tool taps are
not gated.
---
diff --git a/include/config/keybind.h b/include/config/keybind.h
--- a/include/config/keybind.h
+++ b/include/config/keybind.h
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@ struct keybind {
 	size_t keycodes_len;
 	int keycodes_layout;
 	bool allow_when_locked;
+	bool allow_when_inhibited;
 	struct wl_list actions;  /* struct action.link */
 	struct wl_list link;     /* struct rcxml.keybinds */
 	bool on_release;
diff --git a/include/labwc.h b/include/labwc.h
--- a/include/labwc.h
+++ b/include/labwc.h
@@ -384,6 +384,14 @@ void seat_pointer_end_grab(struct seat *seat, struct wlr_surface *surface);
 void seat_focus_lock_surface(struct seat *seat, struct wlr_surface *surface);
 
 void seat_set_focus_layer(struct seat *seat, struct wlr_layer_surface_v1 *layer);
+
+/*
+ * True while the layer-shell surface that captures input for another machine
+ * holds the keyboard exclusively. Every key and button is then meant for that
+ * machine: only keybinds marked allowWhenInhibited run, no mousebind runs and
+ * no menu or window-switcher key is handled.
+ */
+bool seat_bindings_inhibited(struct seat *seat);
 void seat_output_layout_changed(struct seat *seat);
 
 /*
diff --git a/src/config/rcxml.c b/src/config/rcxml.c
--- a/src/config/rcxml.c
+++ b/src/config/rcxml.c
@@ -565,6 +565,7 @@ fill_keybind(xmlNode *node)
 	lab_xml_get_bool(node, "onRelease", &keybind->on_release);
 	lab_xml_get_bool(node, "layoutDependent", &keybind->use_syms_only);
 	lab_xml_get_bool(node, "allowWhenLocked", &keybind->allow_when_locked);
+	lab_xml_get_bool(node, "allowWhenInhibited", &keybind->allow_when_inhibited);
 
 	append_parsed_actions(node, &keybind->actions);
 }
diff --git a/src/input/cursor.c b/src/input/cursor.c
--- a/src/input/cursor.c
+++ b/src/input/cursor.c
@@ -659,6 +659,10 @@ cursor_process_motion(struct server *server, uint32_t time, double *sx, double *
 			 * moving/resizing the wrong view
